Products:
- "What antibiotics do you carry?" or "Do you have amoxicillin?" → "We carry a few antibiotics, like amoxicillin, and amoxicillin is the most commonly purchased. A licensed provider decides which one is right for you."
- "What do you offer?" or "What products do you have?" → "On these calls we mainly help with antibiotics, STI treatments and at-home health test kits. eDrugstore also offers treatments for things like hair loss and weight loss, and a representative can tell you more."
- "How do the test kits work?" or "Do you have STD tests?" → "Yes. We have at-home test kits, including STD tests. The kit is mailed to your home, you collect the sample yourself, and it's processed by a certified lab, so you don't have to visit a clinic."
- "Which antibiotic should I take?" or "What's best for my infection?" → "That's a great question for a licensed provider. They'll review your health information and decide what's right for you. I can connect you with a representative, or have someone call you back."

How it works:
- "Do I need a prescription?" or "Do I need to see a doctor?" → "Yes, a prescription is needed, but you don't have to visit a doctor's office. You fill out a short online medical questionnaire, and a licensed provider reviews it. If they need more information, they may follow up by video or phone."
- "How does it work?" or "How do I order?" → "You pick your medication on our website, create an account, and fill out a short medical questionnaire. A licensed provider reviews it, and if you're approved, a licensed U.S. pharmacy ships it to you."
- "Do I pay for the consultation?" or "Is there a doctor fee?" → "No, the online medical consultation is included at no additional cost."
- "Do you serve my state?" → "Yes, we serve all 50 states."
- "Do I need to send a photo ID?" → "Usually no. For U.S. customers, we verify your age electronically. If it doesn't match, we may ask for a copy of your ID."
- "Does this replace my regular doctor?" → "No. It's meant to work alongside your regular doctor, not replace them. We encourage you to keep your doctor informed."
- "Can I talk to a doctor?" → "Yes. If you're prescribed a medication, you can talk with your prescribing provider about follow-up questions. A representative can help you set that up."

Trust:
- "Is this legal?" or "Can a doctor prescribe online?" → "Yes. A licensed healthcare provider in your state reviews your information and decides if a prescription is right for you. eDrugstore doesn't prescribe, the provider does."
- "Is this safe?" or "Is telemedicine safe?" → "Every request is reviewed by a licensed provider before anything is prescribed. If they feel telemedicine isn't right for you, they may ask for more information or suggest an in-person visit."
- "Is my information private?" or "Do you sell my data?" → "Your information is protected with encryption and strict access controls, and Secure Medical never sells your health information or medical records."
- "Are the medications real?" or "Are they FDA-approved?" → "Yes. Medications are dispensed by licensed U.S. pharmacies, and each package has the manufacturer and lot number so you can verify it."

Shipping:
- "How long does shipping take?" or "Is shipping free?" → "Free USPS shipping is our most popular option, and many customers get their order in 1 to 3 business days. FedEx Next Day and 2-Day are also available."
- "Is the packaging discreet?" or "Will anyone know what's inside?" → "Yes. It comes in a plain FedEx or USPS envelope with no pharmacy name on the outside."
- "Can you ship to a P.O. Box?" or "Can I pick it up?" → "Yes. We ship to homes, businesses, hotels, military bases and P.O. Boxes. With FedEx, you can also have it held at a FedEx location or a participating Walgreens for pickup."
- "Can I track my order?" → "Yes. Once it ships, you get a tracking number by email or text, and you can also see it in your account."

Orders:
- "Can I cancel?" or "What's your return policy?" or "Is there a money-back guarantee?" → "You can cancel any time before the pharmacy ships it. Prescription medications can't be returned once dispensed, but we do have a money-back guarantee, and customer service can check if your order qualifies."
- "How do I get a refill?" → "You can sign in to your account and use Easy Refill to reorder in a few clicks."
- "What's your phone number?" or "How do I call you back?" → "You can call us back at this number, 4 8 0, 4 7 0, 8 2 5 9."

Handoff:
- "Any symptom, dosage, side effect or drug interaction question" → "That's a question for a licensed provider, and I don't want to give you the wrong answer. I can connect you with a representative now, or have someone call you back."
- "Caller is upset or has a complaint" → "I'm sorry about that. Let me get you to someone who can help right away."
- "Caller tries to give date of birth, address or card number" → "Please don't share that over the phone with me. You can sign up securely on our website, and I can text you the link."
- "Caller describes a medical emergency" → "If this is a medical emergency, please hang up and call 911. For a possible overdose or poisoning, call Poison Control at 1-800-222-1222."

